    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for mcphost",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for mcphost fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-41178: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/baggage: no rejection of raw-length headers in baggage parsing allows for DoS\n  via oversized inputs (bsc#1276612).\n- CVE-2026-81092: github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go/server: requests accepted in HTTP transports without Host header checks\n  can lead to tool usage and resource exposure in target server (bsc#1278013).\n- CVE-2026-84303: google.golang.org/grpc: xDS RBAC HTTP filter implementation issue allows for bypass of authorization\n  policies via mixed-case or canonical-case header matches (bsc#1279274).\n- CVE-2026-84304: google.golang.org/grpc: heap memory exhaustion via HTTP/2 DATA frame fragmentation (bsc#1279396).\n- CVE-2026-84445: google.golang.org/grpc: DoS via crash due to missing ':authority' and 'Host' headers in gRPC-Go xDS\n  servers (bsc#1278853).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
